@ 10.3.3 - Proto-Oceanic to Lemerig
# citation: thetha, from François, Alexander (2005), “Unraveling the history of the vowels of seventeen north Vanuatu languages” thetha says “intervening consonants sometimes optional in the [following] sound changes”:
	{ p, pʷ, k, q } > { β, w, ɣ, ∅ }
	VV > V
	{ ndr, *R } > { d, r }
	{ {c,*j}, ɲ } > { s, n }
	t > ʔ “often”
	{ b, bʷ, d, ɡ } > { p, kpʷ, t, k }
	mʷ > ŋmʷ
	— iCV:[-high] > aC
	— eCV:[+mid] > ɛC
	— eCV:[+low] > aC
	— aCV:[+high] > {ɛ,œ}C
	— aCa > {ɘ,a}C
	— oCV:[+high] > øC
	{ —, oCo } > { œC, (sporadic) }
	— oCV:[-high] > ɔC
	— uCV:[-high] > oC
	{ o, e } > { ʊ, ɪ }
	ia > ɪ “(only somoetimes?)”
	V > ∅ / #_CV
	V > ∅ / CVC_CV
	CVC”V > CVC”V